  "b6_reason": "rms speed increased BY 3 times means new speed = 4x old speed (v_old + 3v_old); since v_rms is proportional to sqrt(T), T scales by 4^2=16.",
  "b6_working": "T1 = -50+273 = 223 K. v2 = 4 v1 (increased by 3 times = old + 3x old). T2/T1 = (v2/v1)^2 = 16. T2 = 16 x 223 = 3568 K = 3568 - 273 = 3295 degC.",
  "b6_confidence": "high",
  "b6_note": "Phrase 'increased by 3 times' is ambiguous (could mean v2=3v1 giving T2=1734 degC, matching no option) vs v2=4v1 (old + 3x increase) giving T2=3295 degC, which matches option 2 exactly, so that is the intended reading.",
